- 4. Review terminology and language adaptation.
- 8. Evaluate results and record improvements.
- - Links are relevant and lead to credible sources.
- - Reporting explains the limitations of available data.
- - Confidential and personal information is handled appropriately.
- - The tone remains neutral, informative, and non-promotional.
- ## Output Style
- Use clear, professional, educational language. Avoid sales claims, exaggerated benefits, unsupported statistics, keyword stuffing, and unnecessary repetition.
